e prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs 75 years, and August to September and September to October each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them. In 2025, August to September on the middle of the grids came in at 44% of normal and November to December at 48%, while May to June hit 181%. So far in 2026, May to June came in at 76% of normal. Grid 24211 had its driest year in 2001 at 64% of normal.</p>"}
